      "worked": "Each traveller has 3 choices, giving $3^5$ unrestricted assignments.\n\nFor each of the 3 cabins, $2^5$ assignments leave that cabin empty. Subtract these, then add back the 3 assignments with two cabins empty, which were subtracted twice.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=3^5-3\\times2^5+3\\times1^5\\\\N&=243-96+3\\\\N&=150.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThere are 150 ways.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
